# LF everywhere, on every platform. This repo has ZERO tracked .bat/.cmd (the one category that
# requires CRLF), `.editorconfig` already mandates `end_of_line = lf`, and Prettier defaults to LF — so
# the 185 CRLF files that existed before 2026-07-29 were a Windows-authoring artifact violating the
# project's own standard, silently reformatted on every Prettier run. `text=auto` stores LF in the blob
# on add (so CRLF cannot re-enter a commit for a text file); `eol=lf` forces LF on checkout regardless
# of core.autocrlf/core.eol. `.githooks/pre-commit` CHECK 3 is the backstop. Measured, not guessed.
* text=auto eol=lf

packages/core/src/database/migration.gen.ts linguist-generated

# Git hooks are run through `sh`. A CRLF shebang line makes sh report "bad interpreter" and the hook
# then silently never runs — which is the exact failure mode `.githooks/` exists to remove, so pin the
# line endings rather than relying on every clone having core.autocrlf=false.
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalized (a corrupted PNG test fixture cost us). `text=auto`
# above already protects anything git detects as binary via the NUL heuristic; these are the extensions
# where that detection is not worth trusting — an audio/native/font asset misread as text would corrupt.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.icns binary
*.mp3 binary
*.aac binary
*.dll binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
